# Firmware: version bumps and OTA

The **user** decides when firmware is versioned or flashed to hardware. The agent does **not** bump versions or run OTA/USB uploads unless they **clearly ask in that conversation** (e.g. “patch bump and OTA”, “flash my device”, “upload to spa-…”).

## Do not without explicit ask

- Change **`VERSION`** in [`src/main.h`](src/main.h) or cut a release section in [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) for shipping
- Run **`pio run -e <env> -t upload`**, **`espota`**, or other commands that **flash firmware** to a tub device
- Run **`pio run -e <env> -t uploadfs`** unless the user asked to flash filesystem assets

## OK without asking (implementation and verification)

- Edit firmware/libs, run **`pio run -e <env>`** (compile only)
- Read-only checks: **`GET /api/version`**, MQTT subscribe, serial monitor, **`git status`** / **`git diff`**
- Summarize changes and **remind** the user when they may want to version or flash (e.g. “bump version and OTA when you’re ready”)

## When the user asks to flash

- Confirm **environment** (`M5AtomLite-tub`, `M5AtomLite-tub-ota`, etc.) and **target** if ambiguous
- Version/changelog updates belong in the **same** request only if they asked for both

Project context: [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md), [`platformio.ini`](platformio.ini).
